    questions: [
      PracticeQuestion(
scenario:
"Question 1: (a) Explain four reasons why students abuse drugs.\n"
"(b) State three effects of substance abuse.\n"
"(BECE 2005 Q4)",
answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Answer:\n"
"⦿ Refusal to follow professional medical guidance: Some students reject qualified medical counsel and choose self-medication instead of seeking proper healthcare advice.\n"
"⦿ Impact of emotional distress: Difficult emotions like shyness, anxiety, or internal stress can push young people to use drugs to regulate how they feel.\n"
"⦿ Ignorance regarding drug hazards: A lack of awareness concerning the dangerous physical and mental outcomes of illicit substances leads many students to experiment blindly.\n"
"⦿ Influence of peer groups: Pressure from social circles or observing friends indulging in drug habits creates strong pressure on students to imitate them.\n"
"⦿ Economic hardship: Situations involving extreme poverty, unemployment, or financial stress in families can lead students toward drug use as a coping mechanism.\n\n"
"Answer: (b)\n"
"⦿ Severe physical health damage: Irresponsible drug consumption harms critical bodily organs, leading to conditions like heart failure, lung damage, or stroke.\n"
"⦿ Impaired mental health and cognitive function: Regular substance misuse damages brain tissues, causing memory loss, psychosis, or chronic mental instability.\n"
"⦿ Social and behavioural disruption: Substance abuse often results in addiction, truancy, involvement in criminal activities, and ruined personal relationships.",
explanation: ".",
),
