    questions: [
      PracticeQuestion(
scenario:
"Question 1: (a) What is Salat? Mention the five compulsory daily prayers and the period each is offered.\n"
"(b) State three moral values of Salat.\n"
"(BECE 2000 Q1b)",
answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Answer:\n"
"⦿ Salat stands as the formal obligatory ritual devotion rendered by Muslims, serving as the second core pillar of Islamic faith.\n"
"⦿ Fajr is observed at dawn before sunrise occurs.\n"
"⦿ Zuhr is performed during early afternoon hours right after the sun passes its zenith.\n"
"⦿ Asr takes place in the late afternoon prior to sunset.\n"
"⦿ Maghrib is observed immediately following the setting of the sun.\n"
"⦿ Isha is performed during the night once evening twilight completely vanishes.\n\n"
"Answer: (b)\n"
"⦿ Participating in regular prayer fosters a pardoning disposition among believers, inspiring mutual reconciliation and peaceful living.\n"
"⦿ Systematic worship strengthens the spiritual link connecting the worshipper to the Almighty, ensuring religious principles govern everyday choices.\n"
"⦿ Routine devotion acts as a constant reminder for individuals to distance themselves from improper habits, dishonesty, and immoral conduct.",
explanation: "",
),
PracticeQuestion(
scenario:
"Question 2: (a) Describe how Salat is performed.\n"
"(b) State three moral values of Salat.\n"
"(BECE 2000 Q2)",
answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Answer:\n"
"⦿ The individual begins by establishing ritual purity through ablution, laying out a clean mat, standing to face the Qiblah, and quietly forming the intention to pray.\n"
"⦿ The worshipper raises both hands level with the ears while proclaiming \"Allah Akbar\", subsequently placing the right hand over the left across the chest.\n"
"⦿ The opening chapter of the Holy Qur'an, known as Suratul Fatiha, is recited alongside additional scriptural verses while maintaining a standing posture.\n"
"⦿ The person bows at the waist with hands resting on the knees, proclaiming adoration through the phrase \"Glory to my Lord the greatest\".\n"
"⦿ Returning briefly to an upright standing stance, the individual descends into prostration by placing forehead, nose, palms, knees, and toes on the mat while affirming \"Glory to my Lord the most high\".\n"
"⦿ The worshipper sits back on the heels to recite testimonial prayers, completing the service by turning the head rightward and leftward with greetings of peace.\n\n"
"Answer: (b)\n"
"⦿ Adhering to fixed daily prayer schedules instils personal order, focus, and self-restraint.\n"
"⦿ Prostrating before the Creator highlights that every human being shares equal standing regardless of material wealth or social rank.\n"
"⦿ Gathering for group prayers builds strong communal bonds, mutual care, and solidarity among participants.",
explanation: "",
),
