PracticeQuestion(
scenario:
"Question 4: Describe how Wudu (Ablution) in Islam is made.\n"
"(BECE 2001 Q2)",
answer: "Correct Answer: Answer:\n"
"⦿ The worshipper initiates the process with a pure mind, declaring the intention for ritual cleansing and uttering \"Bismillah-ar-Rahman-ar-Rahim\".\n"
"⦿ Both hands are washed up to the wrist joint three times, followed by thoroughly rinsing the mouth three times.\n"
"⦿ Water is drawn gently into the nostrils and expelled three times, after which the entire face is washed from forehead to chin three times.\n"
"⦿ The right forearm is washed up to the elbow three times, followed by the left forearm, before wiping wet hands gently over the top of the head.\n"
"⦿ The inner and outer areas of both ears are wiped using wet fingers, ending with washing the right foot up to the ankle three times, followed by the left foot.",
explanation: "",
),
