PracticeQuestion(
scenario:
"Question 5: (a) Give four reasons why one should support religious groups with one's money.\n"
"(b) List four instances where such monies are misused by religious leaders.\n"
"(BECE 2006 Q7)",
answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Reasons for supporting religious groups financially:\n"
"⦿ To fund the smooth growth, expansion, and administrative upkeep of religious bodies.\n"
"⦿ To enable religious groups to initiate and finance profitable investments such as treasury bills and estate development.\n"
"⦿ To empower religious institutions to meet their financial obligations and charitable commitments.\n"
"⦿ To assist religious groups in establishing developmental projects such as schools, clinics, and hospitals.\n"
"⦿ To support the training of future leaders and religious ministers through workshops and seminars.\n\n"
"(b) Instances where monies are misused by religious leaders:\n"
"⦿ Improper financial accounting: Failing to maintain accurate record books or concealing transactions from church members.\n"
"⦿ Embezzlement and collusion: Plotting with a few individuals to secretly divert institutional funds into private accounts.\n"
"⦿ Bribery and corrupt practices: Offering or accepting funds unlawfully to secure personal favors or influence.\n"
"⦿ Over-invoicing: Artificially inflating the costs of goods or services purchased for religious organizations to pocket the difference.\n"
"⦿ Extravagant personal spending: Expending shared funds on unnecessary personal luxuries, excessive travel, or private assets.",
explanation: "",
),
PracticeQuestion(
scenario:
"Question 6: (a) State three types of work carried out in your community.\n"
"(b) Give four advantages of working hard.\n"
"(BECE 2007 Q7)",
answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Types of work in the community:\n"
"⦿ Domestic or household work: Daily home tasks such as sweeping, cooking, fetching water, and washing utensils.\n"
"⦿ Occupational or professional work: Career pursuits such as teaching, farming, nursing, driving, and carpentry aimed at earning a livelihood.\n"
"⦿ Community or voluntary service: Shared developmental efforts like cleaning public spaces, building community centers, or organizing local security patrols.\n\n"
"(b) Advantages of working hard:\n"
"⦿ It helps individuals build self-reliance and gain economic independence.\n"
"⦿ It brings social recognition, respect, and high esteem within the local community.\n"
"⦿ It enables workers to earn adequate income to support personal and family needs.\n"
"⦿ It prevents individuals from falling into social vices, crime, and financial dependency.",
explanation: "",
),
PracticeQuestion(
scenario:
"Question 7: (a) Outline four effects of idleness.\n"
"(b) Mention four advantages of enjoying holidays and vacations.\n"
"(BECE 2008 Q8)",
answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Effects of idleness:\n"
"⦿ It frequently lures individuals into dishonourable behaviors such as cheating, stealing, and bribery.\n"
"⦿ It forces people into unhealthy dependency on others for basic survival.\n"
"⦿ It creates room for envy, jealousy, and resentment toward hardworking peers.\n"
"⦿ It results in poverty, hunger, and acute financial hardship.\n"
"⦿ It induces mental stress, anxiety, and loss of self-respect.\n\n"
"(b) Advantages of enjoying holidays and vacations:\n"
"⦿ They provide students and workers an opportunity to assist parents and relatives with domestic duties.\n"
"⦿ They offer ample time for physical rest, relaxation, and mental rejuvenation.\n"
"⦿ They allow people to spend quality bonding time with family members and close friends.\n"
"⦿ They provide time to reflect on past performance and plan effectively for upcoming academic or work terms.",
explanation: "",
),
PracticeQuestion(
scenario:
"Question 8: (a) Mention four reasons why money should be kept out of children's reach.\n"
"(b) In what four ways do people misuse money in your community?\n"
"(BECE 2009 Q8)",
answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Reasons why money should be kept out of children's reach:\n"
"⦿ Soiled or dirty cash can carry harmful bacteria and transmit health infections to young children.\n"
"⦿ Children might accidentally tear, damage, or destroy paper currency notes.\n"
"⦿ Small coins pose severe choking hazards if infants put them in their mouths.\n"
"⦿ Early unrestricted access to cash can tempt young children into developing bad spending habits or stealing.\n\n"
"(b) Ways people misuse money in the community:\n"
"⦿ Engaging in illegal gambling, betting, or lotteries.\n"
"⦿ Expending hard-earned income on alcohol, drugs, or smoking products.\n"
"⦿ Offering bribes to bypass official processes or obtain undeserved favors.\n"
"⦿ Spending excessively on lavish social events, celebrations, or showy displays.",
explanation: "",
),
PracticeQuestion(
scenario:
"Question 9: (a) What is leisure?\n"
"(b) Give five reasons why leisure is important to people.\n"
"(BECE 2011 Q8)",
answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Definition of leisure:\n"
"⦿ Leisure refers to period of free time when an individual is completely released from official work, academic studies, or compulsory domestic duties.\n\n"
"(b) Importance of leisure:\n"
"⦿ It allows the body and mind to rest, regain lost physical energy, and rebuild strength.\n"
"⦿ It helps reduce physical stress, mental tension, and emotional fatigue accumulated from hard work.\n"
"⦿ It grants individuals the opportunity to engage in creative hobbies and recreational activities.\n"
"⦿ It fosters social interaction and strengthens relationships with family members and friends.\n"
"⦿ It enhances productivity by enabling people to return to their normal duties refreshed and energized.",
explanation: "",
),
