),
PracticeQuestion(
scenario:
"Question 18: (a) State four acceptable ways of saving money.\n"
"(b) Explain four reasons for which it is wrong to give bribe.\n"
"(BECE 2023 Q8)",
answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Acceptable ways of saving money:\n"
"⦿ Commercial banks: Depositing money into savings or current accounts for safety and interest accumulation.\n"
"⦿ Mobile money wallets: Storing digital funds securely on registered telecom financial services.\n"
"⦿ Credit unions and Susu: Participating in organized community rotating savings schemes.\n"
"⦿ Home piggy banks: Keeping spare cash securely locked inside a home money box for short-term needs.\n\n"
"(b) Reasons why giving bribes is wrong:\n"
"⦿ It violates moral and religious laws: Bribing distorts justice and goes against divine principles of truthfulness.\n"
"⦿ It is an illegal offense: Giving or taking bribes breaks national laws and can lead to prosecution and imprisonment.\n"
"⦿ It discourages merit and hard work: Bribes allow unqualified individuals to gain positions over deserving candidates.\n"
"⦿ It creates public mistrust: Corrupt practices ruin faith in public institutions and retard overall national development.",
