      PracticeQuestion(
        scenario:
        "Question 1: (a) Describe the early life of Prophet Mohammed.\n"
            "(b) Indicate three moral lessons that can be learnt from his life.\n"
            "(BECE 1999 Q2)",
        answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Answer:\n"
            "⦿ The founder of the Islamic faith was born on 20th April, 571 A.D. within the city of Mecca.\n"
            "⦿ His father Abdullah passed away prior to his birth, while his mother Amina died when he reached six years of age.\n"
            "⦿ Following the loss of his mother, his grandfather Abdul Mutalib cared for him, naming him Mohammed to signify \"the praised one\".\n"
      "⦿ Upon the passing of his grandfather two years later, his uncle Abu Talib assumed responsibility for his upbringing.\n"
      "⦿ During his youth, he engaged in commercial trips alongside his uncle to Syria, where a Christian monk identified him as a future prophet and cautioned against remaining in Syria due to potential harm from hostile groups.\n"
      "⦿ In his adulthood, he earned recognition for his quiet, calm, dignified, and trustworthy demeanor, eventually managing the business ventures of a wealthy widow named Khadijah, whom he married at twenty-five years of age.\n\n"
      "Answer: (b)\n"
      "⦿ Hard Work and Dedication: He demonstrated a strong work ethic throughout his youth, showing commitment and diligence in every undertaking.\n"
        "⦿ Truthfulness and Honesty: His transparent conduct in business transactions earned him the title Al-Ameen, reflecting his absolute integrity when dealing with others.\n"
        "⦿ Humility and Prayerfulness: He maintained a modest lifestyle regardless of his position and devoted significant time to spiritual reflection and prayer.",
        explanation: "",
      ),
