        "Question 7: (a) Describe the call of Moses by God.\n"
            "(b) What three lessons can be learnt from the life of Moses?\n"
            "(BECE 2014 Q1)",
        answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Answer:\n"
            "⦿ While tending the flock of his father-in-law Jethro near Mount Horeb, Moses noticed a bush that was engulfed in flames yet remained unconsumed by the fire.\n"
            "⦿ Surprised by this strange sight, Moses moved closer to inspect the bush, at which point God called out his name from within the flames.\n"
            "⦿ God instructed Moses to remove his sandals because the ground he was standing on was holy terrain.\n"
            "⦿ God revealed that He had seen the suffering of the Israelites in Egypt and was sending Moses to Pharaoh to lead His people out of bondage.\n"
            "⦿ Although Moses initially expressed self-doubt regarding his ability to lead, God reassured him of His presence and assigned Aaron to assist him as a spokesman.\n\n"
            "Answer: (b)\n"
            "⦿ Humility and Obedience: Moses submitted to divine instruction despite his initial feelings of inadequacy.\n"
            "⦿ Perseverance: He displayed great patience and resilience while leading a challenging group of people through difficult circumstances.\n"
            "⦿ Leadership and Courage: He boldly confronted powerful authorities to advocate for the freedom and justice of his people.",
        explanation: "",
