      PracticeQuestion(
        scenario:
        "Question 8: (a) Write on how Joseph came to live in Egypt.\n"
            "(b) Mention four moral lessons learnt from the story.\n"
            "(BECE 2015 Q1)",
        answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Answer:\n"
            "⦿ Joseph was the favored son of Jacob, who presented him with an ornate coat of many colors, causing his brothers to feel deep jealousy toward him.\n"
            "⦿ His brothers' resentment grew stronger when Joseph shared dreams that indicated he would one day rule over them.\n"
            "⦿ When Jacob sent Joseph to check on his brothers in the fields, they plotted to kill him, but Reuben persuaded them to throw him into a dry pit instead.\n"
            "⦿ While Reuben was away, a caravan of Ishmaelite traders passed by, and the brothers sold Joseph to them for twenty pieces of silver.\n"
            "⦿ The traders transported Joseph to Egypt, where he was sold as a servant to Potiphar, an officer of Pharaoh.\n\n"
            "Answer: (b)\n"
            "⦿ Forgiveness: Joseph showed complete willingness to forgive his brothers despite their mistreatment of him.\n"
            "⦿ Trust in God: Maintaining faith through unfair hardships can ultimately lead to positive outcomes.\n"
            "⦿ Avoidance of Favoritism: Parents should treat all children equally to prevent rivalry and resentment within the family.\n"
            "⦿ Integrity: Standing firm against temptations preserves moral character even in difficult environments.",
        explanation: "",
